  "source_changes": [
    "Register actual dedicated shared references only after successful acquisition; reset the reference ContextVar before finally releasing. Preserve independent idempotent rollback/close.",
    "Capture the original dedicated PID and PG transaction identity; acquisition and every matching reuse verify own PID, transaction, exact namespace/key, objsubid=2, granted ShareLock. Verification does not clear acquired; repeat acquire verifies continuity and released references cannot reconnect.",
    "Reuse raw same-key references before the application atomic branch, verify tracked reuse and cached assertions, recheck live gate state and set runtime bookkeeping during reuse yield. SQL-owned context semantics remain unchanged.",
    "Refuse exclusive runtime boundaries under any retained raw reference including P=0 before dedicated exclusive connection creation; preserve exclusive owner and counter semantics.",
    "Before new tenant admission, combine verified actual raw keys with existing runtime keys, excluding P=0. Refuse all lower-new-key cases before acquiring any new N and provide a central administration origin retry hint. Continue sorted admission and live state checks for every DB-derived membership regardless of status."
  ],
